{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N1x9koc8U2SxpkPWNztTtc","type":"tool_result","content":"0\tdream_id: dream_20260520T185426\n1\tproject: ec_hte_llm_annotation\n2\tvenue: ''\n3\tfocus: 核心关注：(1) \"debiasing can hurt\" 的 surprise value 是否足够撑起 EMNLP main；(2) 层级贝叶斯\n4\t  partial pooling 作为方法核心是否有足够技术贡献；(3) 仅有合成+半合成实验时论文是否可接受（Ashwin 数据集可能拿不到）；(4) 与 PPCI\n5\t  (Sui 2026) 的差异化是否清晰\n6\treview_mode: full\n7\treview_visible: true\n8\twriting_visible: true\n9\twhat_if: []\n10\ttier_definitions:\n11\t  tiers:\n12\t    best:\n13\t      tier: best\n14\t      meaning: 三条 claims 全部在合理参数范围内得到强验证；semi-synthetic 结果足够 dramatic 撑 headline；Ashwin\n15\t        数据可用或可替代\n16\t      key_assumptions:\n17\t      - global correction 在 moderate heterogeneity 设定下即产生显著 bias 放大（不需要极端参数）\n18\t      - HB partial pooling 在 n_expert=250 时已明显优于 stratified MLE（小样本优势可量化）\n19\t      - diagnostic criterion 有高判别力，阈值跨数据集稳定\n20\t      - semi-synthetic 中 GPT-4.1/Qwen3 的 misclassification heterogeneity 自然存在且足够大\n21\t      - 至少有一个 real-data 验证（Ashwin 或替代公开数据集）\n22\t      number_ranges:\n23\t        bias_amplification_factor_global_vs_uncorrected:\n24\t        - 5.0\n25\t        - 12.0\n26\t        ec_hte_absolute_cate_bias:\n27\t        - 0.005\n28\t        - 0.02\n29\t        ec_hte_coverage_90ci:\n30\t        - 0.9\n31\t        - 0.97\n32\t        min_n_expert_for_dominance:\n33\t        - 100\n34\t        - 250\n35\t        diagnostic_criterion_auroc:\n36\t        - 0.9\n37\t        - 0.98\n38\t        hb_vs_stratified_mle_bias_reduction:\n39\t        - 0.3\n40\t        - 0.6\n41\t        ec_hte_vs_ppci_bias_ratio:\n42\t        - 0.15\n43\t        - 0.4\n44\t      narrative_direction: '原始 framing 完全成立。\"Debiasing can hurt\" 作为 problem-level\n45\t        discovery 有足够 surprise value： 在 realistic 参数下 global correction 使 bias 恶化\n46\t        5-10x，这是 NLP+CSS 社区未意识到的陷阱。 EC-HTE 以 250 expert labels 实现 near-oracle，HB partial\n47\t        pooling 的小样本优势可量化。 Diagnostic criterion 作为 standalone practical tool 给论文第三条独立贡献。\n48\t        Real data 验证锁定了 \"不只是理论上可能\" 的叙事。投 EMNLP main 无需降级任何 claim。\n49\t\n50\t        '\n51\t    median:\n52\t      tier: median\n53\t      meaning: bias 放大效应存在但幅度中等，需更多 expert labels 才稳定；仅有合成+半合成验证；PPCI 区分度存在但不悬殊\n54\t      key_assumptions:\n55\t      - global correction bias 放大在 moderate heterogeneity 下可复现，但倍数不如极端设定 dramatic\n56\t      - HB partial pooling 优于 MLE 的优势仅在 n_expert<500 时显著，大样本下差异收敛\n57\t      - diagnostic criterion 有效但阈值需要 per-dataset 校准，不能直接 transfer\n58\t      - semi-synthetic LLM 自然 heterogeneity 存在但偏温和，需选择特定 subgroup 定义才能放大效应\n59\t      - Ashwin 数据不可用，无 real-data 实验\n60\t      number_ranges:\n61\t        bias_amplification_factor_global_vs_uncorrected:\n62\t        - 2.0\n63\t        - 5.0\n64\t        ec_hte_absolute_cate_bias:\n65\t        - 0.02\n66\t        - 0.05\n67\t        ec_hte_coverage_90ci:\n68\t        - 0.85\n69\t        - 0.92\n70\t        min_n_expert_for_dominance:\n71\t        - 250\n72\t        - 500\n73\t        diagnostic_criterion_auroc:\n74\t        - 0.78\n75\t        - 0.9\n76\t        hb_vs_stratified_mle_bias_reduction:\n77\t        - 0.1\n78\t        - 0.3\n79\t        ec_hte_vs_ppci_bias_ratio:\n80\t        - 0.4\n81\t        - 0.7\n82\t      narrative_direction: '需要调整 claims 强度。Claim 1 从 \"debiasing can hurt 5-10x\" 软化为\n83\t        \"debiasing can hurt, 且 hurt 的程度随 heterogeneity product 单调增长\"——强调 mechanism\n84\t        的 monotonic relationship 而非绝对倍数。Claim 2 中 \"250 expert labels\" 上调为 \"500\"，partial\n85\t        pooling 的叙事从 \"dramatically better\" 转为 \"principled regularization with guaranteed\n86\t        non-inferiority\"。 Claim 3 的 diagnostic 从 \"computable threshold\" 弱化为 \"computable\n87\t        risk score + decision heuristic\"。无 real data 需在 limitation 中正面处理，并在 semi-synthetic\n88\t        设计上加强 ecological validity 论证（real corpus, real LLM errors, only treatment\n89\t        effect is synthetic）。 仍可投 EMNLP main，但需补充：(a) 更细粒度的 sensitivity analysis 替代\n90\t        dramatic headline number, (b) partial pooling 的理论 shrinkage 分析（bias-variance\n91\t        tradeoff 可视化）。\n92\t\n93\t        '\n94\t    worst:\n95\t      tier: worst\n96\t      meaning: bias 放大效应仅在极端/人造参数下显著，realistic 设定中 global correction 仍可接受；HB 无明显优势；需要\n97\t        reframe\n98\t      key_assumptions:\n99\t      - bias 放大仅在 misclass heterogeneity 极端时出现（Δ error rate > 0.3），moderate 设定下 global"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017CF8j9mavTxWyd4xGEWngg","session_id":"243f7ab5-0b31-4460-862b-4acef4243b5d","uuid":"4eebe6ad-9cdc-4303-9db6-e4abc41729f7","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:18:26.792Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Xx3MwAo6zdLH2A2eoTRBN","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\\\\n- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\\\\n- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \\\\\\\"debiasing\\\\\\\" can worsen CATE bias by 5-10x compared to no correction at all.\\\\n\\\\n2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) eliminates this bias while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. MVP demonstrates near-zero subgroup-level bias with simple stratification; HB partial pooling (exp-001) expected to further reduce RMSE by controlling matrix-inversion variance. Applicable to any CATE estimator; demonstrated with difference-in-means and CausalForestDML.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic: when this product exceeds a threshold, global correction is harmful and stratified correction is needed. This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine\\\\n\\\\n- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis (e.g., \\\\\\\"tweet contains economic framing\\\\\\\" moderates campaign effectiveness). LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\\\\n\\\\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\\\\n\\\\n- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \\\\\\\"problem identification + principled solution\\\\\\\" not \\\\\\\"new estimation technique.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- **Headline result template**: \\\\\\\"On semi-synthetic political-science benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by up to 7.8x in low-error subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bias mechanism identification + formal bound**: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity. Includes \\\\\\\"debiasing can hurt\\\\\\\" proposition with constructive example. (Theory + Empirical)\\\\n2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\\\\n3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\\\\n4. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data case study (pattern consistency, not ground-truth benchmark) with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\\\\n\\\\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\\\\n\\\\n1. **\\\\\\\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\\\\\\\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\\\\n\\\\n2. **\\\\\\\"How is this different from PPCI / DSL?\\\\\\\"** — PPCI corrects outcome-side measurement error via kernel localization; we correct covariate-side. Orthogonal, and composable. DSL applied per-subgroup is a valid baseline but lacks cross-subgroup shrinkage, operates at estimand level rather than measurement model level, and has strictly higher variance under partial pooling. Do NOT say \\\\\\\"DSL cannot do subgroup correction\\\\\\\" — say it lacks the principled shrinkage mechanism.\\\\n\\\\n3. **\\\\\\\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\\\\\\\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\\\\n\\\\n4. **\\\\\\\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\\\\\\\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\\\\n\\\\n5. **\\\\\\\"Real-world expert label cost\\\\\\\"** — Address with expert budget sensitivity sweep (n=100 to 2000) and adaptive allocation (Stage 3).\\\\n\\\\n6. **\\\\\\\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\\\\\\\"** — Carroll et al. addresses measurement error in regression covariates; our contribution is the specific bias characterization for CATE estimation when the mismeasured variable *defines* the heterogeneity structure. The Δπ×Δτ product form is a new result in this context. Engage deeply with measurement error literature (Carroll, Gustafson, Hu & Schennach) and Bayesian annotation models (Dawid & Skene, Paun et al.) to contextualize precisely.\\\\n\\\\n7. **\\\\\\\"Methodological novelty is modest\\\\\\\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. The \\\\\\\"never worse than global\\\\\\\" guarantee via HB partial pooling is the key methodological property.\\\\n\\\\n8. **\\\\\\\"Why no figures?\\\\\\\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\n\\\\nEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use case (political messaging, refugee interviews), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track.\\\\n\\\\nRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 7657, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FX1n1RMdseirwuNuQ9WE48","session_id":"243f7ab5-0b31-4460-862b-4acef4243b5d","uuid":"6311cda1-4dc0-47b0-a546-781ccba2a533","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:18:26.580Z"}
